    `[target.'cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")'.dependencies]` with `wasm-bindgen`,
    `wasm-bindgen-futures`, `web-sys` (features `HtmlCanvasElement`, `Window`, `Document`),
    `js-sys`, `console_error_panic_hook`, `console_log` + `log`, `getrandom` (feature `wasm_js`).
  - `.cargo/config.toml` (new) — `[target.wasm32-unknown-unknown] rustflags = ['--cfg',
    'getrandom_backend="wasm_js"']`.
  - `src/lib.rs` — add a `#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")] mod web;` (or inline) placeholder that
    `console_error_panic_hook::set_once()` and exposes a trivial `#[wasm_bindgen]` symbol so the
    cdylib has an entry point (filled out in U4).
  - `.gitignore` — ignore `www/pkg/`.
- **Approach:** Confirm `src/lib.rs` exists (the crate is imported by tests, so it does) and add the
  cfg-gated web module seam. Keep all native deps and examples building. Document the one-time
  prereq `rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown` in a build note (not code).
- **Patterns to follow:** v1 `crates/sim-wasm/Cargo.toml` (`git show main:crates/sim-wasm/Cargo.toml`)
  — same wasm dep set + `crate-type`.
- **Test scenarios:**
  - Covers R1. *Native build unaffected:* `cargo build` and `cargo build --tests` succeed with the
